{
  "title": "Quantum Dynamical Bounds for Long-Range Operators with Skew-Shift Potentials",
  "authors": [
    "Wencai Liu",
    "Matthew Powell",
    "Xueyin Wang"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2411.00176",
  "abstract": "This paper improves the quantum dynamical upper bounds for long-range operators with skew-shift potentials, which are crucial in understanding the behavior of quantum particles. The authors employ Weyl's method and Vinogradov's method to analyze skew-shift dynamics on semi-algebraic sets, leading to novel sublinear bounds and better quantum dynamical upper bounds.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The paper studies the quantum dynamics of long-range operators on the integer lattice, which is crucial in understanding the behavior of quantum particles. The authors focus on a particular family of operators with dynamically-defined potentials, which are associated with the Hamiltonians of quantum particles that evolve according to Schr\u00f6dinger dynamics. The key insight is to employ Weyl's method and Vinogradov's method to analyze skew-shift dynamics on semi-algebraic sets, leading to novel sublinear bounds and better quantum dynamical upper bounds.",
