    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The authors use Weyl's method and Vinogradov's method to estimate exponential sums, which are used to prove sublinear bounds for semi-algebraic sets. These bounds are then used to establish upper bounds on the quantum dynamics of the long-range operators. The process involves several steps, including the decomposition of the square lattice, the application of the Ho\u0308lder inequality, and the use of the Vinogradov's Mean Value Theorem.",
