    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The authors prove that for any \u03c6 with compact support and p > 0, there exists C = C(\u03b5, v, A, b, \u03b3, \u03c4, \u03c6, p) such that <strong>h|X\u0303Hx,\u03c9|p\u03c6i(T) \u2264 C(log T)\u03b4 + \u03b5</strong> and <strong>h|XHx,\u03c9|p\u03c6i(T) \u2264 C(log T)\u03b4 + \u03b5</strong>, where \u03b4 = \u03c4 b\u03c8(b). These results improve upon previous bounds and provide a better understanding of the quantum dynamics of long-range operators.",
